      {
        "id": 1777958,
        "title": "Aegython 2026",
        "seo_url": "https://unstop.com/hackathons/aegython-2026-aeglysai-1777958",
        "type": "hackathons",
        "subtype": "online_coding_challenge",
        "region": "hybrid",
        "status": "LIVE",
        "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Organised by AeglysAI | Free Participation | Individual and Team Entries</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AEGYTHON 2026 is an AI/ML and Cybersecurity hackathon that challenges students, developers, engineers, and researchers to build practical, intelligent solutions for real-world problems. Participants will explore areas such as identity security, anomaly detection, API traffic monitoring, security alert explanation, outage prediction, and AI-powered solutions for everyday challenges.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The focus is on working prototypes, technical understanding, responsible innovation, and reproducible results&mdash;not just ideas or presentations.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Challenge Areas</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants can choose from six problem statements:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Smart Login Guardian: Identify suspicious login attempts and explain potential risk signals.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Find the Anomaly: Detect unusual patterns in synthetic data or system measurements.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">API Traffic Watch: Identify unusual API request patterns and traffic spikes using synthetic requests.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain My Security Alert: Convert structured security alerts into clear explanations and safe recommendations.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Predict the Outage: Analyse synthetic system metrics to identify early warning signs of possible outages.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AI for Everyday Life: Build a practical AI/ML solution addressing a meaningful everyday problem.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Students, graduate students, early-career engineers, experienced practitioners, and researchers are the intended audience.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Beginners and first-time contributors can explore the Foundation track; experienced participants may pursue more advanced engineering work.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participation is free.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every participant must complete the mandatory individual AeglysAI qualification and be selected before competing.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Age and geographic eligibility must be confirmed in the final official event terms.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Team Formation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants may register individually.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Teams may consist of 1&ndash;4 participants, including the team leader.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every team member must independently complete the qualification process and be selected.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A team leader must submit the team roster for organiser verification and obtain a unique team ID.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants cannot belong to multiple active teams.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Team membership changes require organiser approval.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Inter-college and inter-specialisation teams should be confirmed with the organisers before being advertised as permitted.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Qualification Process</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every participant must demonstrate basic familiarity with the AeglysAI project before selection.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The qualification process involves:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Registering individually through the official form.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Forking the official AeglysAI repository into a personal GitHub account.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cloning the fork and demonstrating that the baseline builds or runs.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Documenting the basic architecture and request/decision flow.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Providing one meaningful technical observation, one realistic improvement idea, and a proposed validation approach.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Submitting the required GitHub links and sanitised build evidence for organiser review.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Completing qualification does not guarantee selection.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Competition Format and Rounds</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 1 &mdash; Technical Screening</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants submit a working project, source code, a README with setup instructions, testing or validation evidence, and a demonstration video of no more than two minutes. Reviewers evaluate the solution's functionality, intelligent features, relevance, reproducibility, and video clarity.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 2 &mdash; Finalist Demonstration</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Shortlisted finalists present their working projects live through Google Meet. Each finalist receives five minutes for the demonstration, followed by five minutes of technical questions and answers.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 2 determines the final ranking. The two rounds are scored separately.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 1 &mdash; 100 points</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Working functionality: 30 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AI/ML or intelligent feature: 25 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Relevance and creativity: 20 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Reproducibility: 15 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Video clarity: 10 points</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 2 &mdash; 100 points</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Live demonstration: 35 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Technical understanding: 25 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Solution quality and safety: 20 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Technical Q&amp;A: 15 points</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Presentation: 5 points</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Final Project Submission Requirements</span></p>\n<p><strong>Each team must submit:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Team ID and selected challenge</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Public GitHub source repository and a fixed review commit or tag</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Project README and reproducible setup instructions</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstration video of up to two minutes</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explanation of the AI/ML or intelligent technique used</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Testing or validation evidence</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Data and model attribution, licensing information, and known limitations</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A slide deck or walkthrough alone is not sufficient. The submission must be a working minimum viable product (MVP), executable prototype, or functional proof of concept. Any programming language or framework may be used.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Competition Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participation is free; no registration fee is required.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every participant must complete individual qualification and selection before competing.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Teams must follow the approved roster and team ID requirements.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Projects must address the selected challenge and demonstrate functional, testable behaviour.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants must submit original work or properly attribute third-party code, data, models, and other resources.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">All submissions must include appropriate setup instructions, testing evidence, and known limitations.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use only systems and data you are authorised to access. Security testing against unauthorised real systems is prohibited.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do not include passwords, credentials, personal information, confidential material, or patent-related private data in public submissions.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants must treat others respectfully, avoid harassment or discrimination, and credit collaborators and prior work.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Judges must disclose conflicts of interest and recuse themselves where appropriate.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Team changes, roster changes, and other exceptions require organiser approval.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Final rankings are determined after Round 2 judging and organiser review. Qualification or registration alone does not guarantee selection, finalist status, a certificate, or an award.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Timeline and Important Information</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The official website currently lists the event dates, deadlines, and final eligibility terms as pending. The organisers should publish the confirmed registration deadline, qualification deadline, project-submission deadline, finalist announcement, and final event date before this listing is approved.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Organiser: AeglysAI</span></p>",
